0011: rows for single-channel 16-bit and packed 10-bit in fd6_ubwc_compat_mode().

Why. The stock fd6_ubwc_compat_mode() (src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h)
has 28 formats with a non-empty case, and among them there is neither a
single-channel 16-bit one nor a packed 10-bit one. Any format list into
which vkd3d puts R16 (and it always does: R16_TYPELESS plus three more
classes) therefore silently loses UBWC.

Silently - because fd6_ubwc_compat_mode() returns FD6_UBWC_UNKNOWN_COMPAT
for them, and tu6_mutable_format_list_ubwc_compatible() exits with false
on the first unknown member. The !mutable_ubwc_fc branch then clears
ubwc_enabled, and the image stays tiled but uncompressed.

This is over-caution, not a hardware limit, and it is measured, not
deduced. Probe CEIL in tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c (logs
results/test-CEIL-base.log and results/test-CEIL-exp0011.log) creates
three images with the same list: a linear one, the same format without a
list, and the same with MUTABLE. A lone R16_UNORM without a list gets
memreq 0x82000 against the linear 0x80000, i.e. the UBWC metadata came
up on its own: the ceiling exists, and it is the gate that removes it.
The same for R10G10B10A2_UNORM: 0x102000 against 0x100000.

Unlike patch 0012, here one does not need to assert that the blob
"allows these, but not a660". Both formats are full citizens of the
texture path: fd6_format_table.c has VTC(R16_UNORM, ..., WZYX) (line 72)
and FMT(R10G10B10A2_UNORM, ..., WZYX) at line 209, both with swap WZYX,
i.e. matching. The gap is only in the compat table, and this is exactly
the case where the argument "all variants of the same block size differ
only in the interpretation of the same bits" holds fully: the layout
depends only on the block size
(layout->cpp = util_format_get_blocksize(), fd6_layout.c:115), as in
0005/0006/0012, and the swap is shared by all members of the list.

What does NOT change. R8_* is deliberately not included here: it has no
ceiling at all. has_8bpp_ubwc = false on gen2 (freedreno_devices.py,
working around the text corruption bug from 0f770caa232, "Disable
8bpp_ubwc on a6xx gen2"), and the measurement confirms it - the
nonmemreq of a lone R8_UNORM equals the linear one. R32G32B32_* as well:
the blob has no 3-component rows and no ceiling shows in the
measurements. These groups are blocked by tu6_ubwc_possible(), not by
the gate, and editing the rule does not fix them.

The format name in the switch. The obvious name is wrong, and it cost
one build: VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32 maps to
PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UNORM (src/vulkan/util/vk_format.c:114), and
PIPE_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM never reaches this switch, even though
such a format exists in p_format.h. The cases hold pipe names, not
Vulkan ones.

What stays out of the patch's scope.
 - fast-clear: a byte roundtrip does not check the clear metadata, as in
   0012.
 - reinterpretation through an R16_UINT view on an R16_TYPELESS list:
   exactly the mechanism that turned out broken in 0010 with diverging
   swaps. Here the swaps of all R16_* match (WZYX), so there will be no
   asymmetry, but it has to be checked separately.
 - Only R10G10B10A2_UNORM and _UINT are added to the compat row, because
   exactly they have tiled entries in fd6_format_table.c (FMT/VTC);
   SNORM, SINT and USCALED have V__ there, i.e. no tiling. If vkd3d
   builds a list with SNORM or SINT, the question runs into the texture
   format table rather than the gate, and this experiment's change will
   not be enough.

Measurement and analysis: docs/analysis.md, section 21.6.

Relations: complements 0006 (same file, other rows) and 0012 (other
format families) - three edits of one compat table, they apply together
without conflicts. The A/B is isolated: git apply -R changes exactly 3
log lines (repeat 04.10.2026: results/test-stack.log vs
results/test-0011.log).

diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@
    FD6_UBWC_R32G32_INT,
    FD6_UBWC_R32G32B32A32_INT,
    FD6_UBWC_R32_FLOAT,
+   FD6_UBWC_R16_INT,
+   FD6_UBWC_A2B10G10R10_INT,
 };
 
 static inline enum fd6_ubwc_compat_type
@@ -82,6 +84,35 @@
    case PIPE_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_SINT:
       return FD6_UBWC_R16G16B16A16_INT;
 
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_UNORM:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_SNORM:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_UINT:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_SINT:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R16_FLOAT:
+      /* The blob table has no single-channel
+       * 16-bit row at all, so every vkd3d list containing R16 (R16_TYPELESS and
+       * three more classes) silently loses UBWC.  Measured on a 740: a lone
+       * R16_UNORM image with no format list does get UBWC metadata
+       * (memreq 0x82000 vs 0x80000 linear), so the ceiling exists and the gate
+       * is what removes it.  All four variants are the same 16 bits read
+       * differently, and the tiled layout is a function of the block size
+       * alone (fd6_layout.c: layout->cpp = util_format_get_blocksize()).
+       */
+      return FD6_UBWC_R16_INT;
+
+   /* NB: vk_to_pipe_format() maps VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32 onto
+    * PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UNORM, not PIPE_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM
+    * (src/vulkan/util/vk_format.c:114), so the R10G10B10A2 spelling is the
+    * one that actually reaches this switch. */
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UNORM:
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UINT:
+      /* Same argument for the packed 10-bit form, and the same measurement:
+       * a lone R10G10B10A2_UNORM image gets 0x102000 against 0x100000 linear.
+       * Only UNORM and UINT are added, and they are exactly the two with a
+       * tiled entry (VTC) in fd6_format_table.c; SNORM and SINT have none.
+       */
+      return FD6_UBWC_A2B10G10R10_INT;
+
    case PIPE_FORMAT_R32_UINT:
    case PIPE_FORMAT_R32_SINT:
       return FD6_UBWC_R32_INT;
